items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-67-[L1] The function limit: $\lim_{x \to c} f(x) = L$ means that for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a real $\delta > 0$ such that every $x \in A$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ satisfies $|f(x) - L| < \varepsilon$ ([[def-function-limit]]).
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-68-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-69-[L2] Sequential convergence: $(y_k) \to y$ means that for every rational $\varepsilon > 0$ there is $K \in \mathbb{N}$ with $|y_k - y| < \varepsilon$ for all $k \ge K$ ([[def-real-limit]], [[def-sequence]]). Testing instead against every positive REAL $\varepsilon$ defines the same relation: every positive rational is a positive real, and below every positive real lies a positive rational ([[lem-rat-embeds-dense]]), which is the passage sanctioned in the remarks of [[def-sequence]].
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-70-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md:71:[L3] Limit point: for every real $\delta > 0$ there is $x \in A$ with $0 < |x - c| < \delta$ ([[def-limit-point-r]], [[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-72-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-73-[L4] Reciprocal Archimedean property: for every real $\varepsilon > 0$ there is a natural $n \ge 1$ with $1/n < \varepsilon$ ([[cor-archimedean-reciprocal]], [[thm-of-archimedean]]); the canonical naturals satisfy $n \cdot 1_{\mathbb{R}} > 0$ and are strictly increasing in $n$ ([[lem-of-naturals-positive]]); and $0 < a < b$ gives $0 < 1/b < 1/a$ ([[lem-of-inverse-positive]]).
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-74-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-75-[L5] Countable choice: for every family $(X_k)_{k \in \mathbb{N}}$ of nonempty sets there is a function $k \mapsto x_k$ with $x_k \in X_k$ for every $k$ ([[def-countable-choice]]).
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-76-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md:77:[L6] Absolute value ([[lem-of-abs-value]]); and trichotomy, so the negation of $|u| < \varepsilon$ is $|u| \ge \varepsilon$, and the negation of "for every $\varepsilon$ there is $\delta$ such that P" is "there is $\varepsilon_0$ such that for every $\delta$, not P" ([[def-ordered-field]]).
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-78-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-79-## Proof
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-80-
items/thm-sequential-criterion-for-function-limits.md-81-**Proof technique:** direct.
