--
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-53-**Given:** The set $A := \{0\} \cup [1,2]$, the constant function $f : A \to \mathbb{R}$ with $f(x) := 0$ for every $x \in A$, and the points $0$ and $1$ of $A$.
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-54-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-55-[L1] The $\varepsilon$-$\delta$ formula displayed above, and the fact that [[def-function-limit]] imposes it only at a limit point of the domain, where [[lem-function-limit-unique]] then makes $L$ unique.
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-56-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md:57:[L2] Limit point and isolated point: $c$ is a limit point of $S$ when $N^{*}_{\rho}(c) \cap S \ne \varnothing$ for every real $\rho > 0$; $c \in S$ is isolated in $S$ when $N_{\rho}(c) \cap S = \{c\}$ for some real $\rho > 0$; and for $c \in S$ the two are exact opposites ([[def-limit-point-r]], [[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-58-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md:59:[L3] Neighbourhoods: $N_{\rho}(u) = \{\, y : |y - u| < \rho \,\}$ and $N^{*}_{\rho}(u) = N_{\rho}(u) \setminus \{u\}$ ([[def-neighbourhood-r]]).
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-60-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-61-[L4] Intervals: $[1,2] = \{\, y : 1 \le y \le 2 \,\}$ ([[def-interval]]).
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-62-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-63-[L5] Absolute value: $|u| \ge 0$; $|u| = 0$ exactly when $u = 0$; $|u| = u$ for $u \ge 0$; $|0| = 0$ ([[lem-of-abs-value]]).
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-64-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md:65:[L6] Order in $\mathbb{R}$: trichotomy and totality; $0 < 1$, so $2 > 0$ and $\rho/2 > 0$ with $\rho/2 < \rho$ for $\rho > 0$; and of two positive reals the smaller is positive ([[cor-of-one-positive]], [[lem-of-add-order]], [[lem-of-sign-rules]], [[def-ordered-field]]).
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-66-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-67-## Counterexample
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-68-
items/cex-limit-not-unique-at-an-isolated-point.md-69-**Proof technique:** direct.
